Three bugs in `courtfill-preview-final.html` — incomplete profile save logic, broken sidebar active state, and a mismatched Monday availability toggle.

## Changes

- **`saveProfile()` only handled `'player'`** — coach and club saves silently no-oped. Added `else if` branches for both roles and added IDs (`coachAvatar`, `coachDisplayName`, `clubAvatar`, `clubDisplayName`) to the view-mode elements so the function can update them:
  ```js
  } else if (role === 'coach') {
    const name = document.getElementById('editCoachName').value.trim()
    document.getElementById('coachDisplayName').textContent = name
    document.getElementById('coachAvatar').textContent = name.charAt(0).toUpperCase()
  } else if (role === 'club') { ... }
  ```

- **`showDashSection()` sidebar highlight always broken** — sidebar items contain emoji icons (e.g. `👤 Profile`), so `textContent` never starts with the plain section name. Changed `startsWith(name)` → `includes(name)`.

- **Monday day-toggle state mismatch** — had `aria-checked="true"` but was missing the `active` CSS class (visual state = OFF), inconsistent with Tuesday. Added the `active` class.

