Adds scheduling API endpoints and supporting infrastructure to power availability slot management (Sculptify) and interview scheduling (March & Lewis), wiring them into both the backend and frontend.

## Backend

- **`middleware/validate.js`** — `requireFields(fields)` middleware; returns `400` with list of missing fields
- **`services/schedulingService.js`** — File-backed CRUD for availability slots and interviews; matches existing `task-engine` persistence pattern
- **`routes/scheduling.js`** — Four endpoints mounted at `/api/scheduling`:
  - `GET /sculptify-availability` / `POST /sculptify-availability` (requires `providerName`, `service`, `slotDate`, `slotTime`)
  - `GET /march-lewis-interviews` / `POST /march-lewis-interviews` (requires `candidateName`, `companyName`, `interviewDate`, `interviewTime`)
- **`server.js`** — Mounts scheduling router at `/api/scheduling`
- **`data/availability.json`**, **`data/interviews.json`** — Empty seed files

## Frontend

- **`apps/sculptify-web/public/app.js`** — Added `loadAvailability()` calling `GET /api/scheduling/sculptify-availability`
- **`apps/march-lewis-web/public/app.js`** — Added `loadInterviews()` calling `GET /api/scheduling/march-lewis-interviews`

## Example

```js
// POST /api/scheduling/sculptify-availability
{ "providerName": "Dr. Smith", "service": "Body Sculpting", "slotDate": "2025-04-01", "slotTime": "10:00 AM" }
// → 201 { ok: true, message: "Availability slot created", slot: { id, ...fields, createdAt } }

// Missing fields → 400 { ok: false, message: "Missing required fields: slotDate, slotTime" }
```

